#### Overview

## What does a premium wellness marketplace need, starting from a name?

Neardeal came to me with only a brand name and a bold vision: to be the next Klook for the beauty industry. In a team of five, I built the branding, the website and the product UI from scratch.

#### Brand

## The logo is a journey, drawn as a leaf.

The logo begins with a leaf, for wellness, nature and growth. Woven into it is the initial N, which also traces an upward path: each user's own wellness journey, a personal line of progress. That path points to a small star at the peak, for the guidance of AI at the core of the platform, which takes repetitive work off staff and offers insight.

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image.webp)

#### Problem

## Premium wellness had no platform that worked for both sides.

The premium beauty and wellness sector had no digital home that could give customers a high-end experience while solving the merchants' day-to-day operations. That meant two problems at once:

{% points %}
{% point title="Customers question the value" text="Premium prices need a premium, frictionless booking to justify them." /%}

{% point title="Merchants drown in operations" text="Rigid pricing empties off-peak hours, while schedules, copy and video all compete for time." /%}
{% /points %}

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-1.webp)

#### Solution

## One marketplace, designed for both sides.

Neardeal is a two-sided marketplace that uses data to serve customers and merchants together.

For customers, a premium, intuitive interface with dynamic pricing that fills off-peak hours, giving users better value and merchants better yield.

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-2.webp)

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-3.webp)

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-4.webp)

For merchants, an AI-integrated dashboard that optimises schedules and handles marketing: it writes package descriptions that convert and helps edit authentic, real-world video quickly.

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-5.webp)

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-6.webp)

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-7.webp)

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-8.webp)

#### Product

## Three apps, one for each person in the booking.

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-9.webp)

#### Customers

## A deal app that still feels premium.

Deals are a large part of the vision, but the beauty industry expects a premium atmosphere, so every button, colour, card and animation is made to delight at first touch. Friction is designed out, like the three-step "book first, pay later" flow, to lift conversion.

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-10.webp)

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-11.webp)

#### Merchants

## A dashboard you can learn without training.

A dashboard does not have to be complex or stuffed into panels. Most staff are not confident with computers, so the dashboard has to explain itself, need minimal training and prevent errors. I chose the copy carefully and tested several variations with real users.

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-12.webp)

#### Staff

## Everything at a glance, nothing to mis-tap.

The staff app's home page is free of distractions: one main action and large text. Staff confirm a booking with a slide gesture, so it cannot happen by accident.

![](/images/experience/neardeal/image-13.webp)
